-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Kiosk stock locations (SFL-046)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- One internal location per kiosk, because a vending machine's stock is physically inside the
-- machine and nowhere else. A kiosk sharing a warehouse location would let one machine reserve
-- goods sitting in another, which is the whole failure the per-kiosk location prevents.
--
-- They carry no warehouse and no parent: a kiosk is not inside a building the business racks, and
-- inventing a hierarchy for it would put a machine on a shelf. Marked is_system_generated because
-- they exist to mirror hardware, not because an operator laid them out.

